-- title:
--   Good points of the ∞-Igusa branch read a place (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and the fields in play are the geometric modular function fields $\overline{M} :=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change, inside Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, of the full level-$M'$ field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`) and $F :=$ `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, together with their characteristic-$q$ counterparts `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` and `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` over the residue field of a valuation ring $A$.
--
--   The data are: a prime $q$ with $q = 2$; a nonzero level $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$; a valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over `ResidueField A` which, by `hW`, consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)` (those places which are rational, affine geometric, and whose value at the geometric $j$-generator lies in the supersingular set `ssJSet q`); the hypothesis `hle` that $\overline{M} \le F$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $\overline{M}$ along $A$ with values in `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of $\overline{M}$ containing the image of $A$ and no more, a surjective residue map onto the characteristic-$q$ field with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with reduction on constants, with the scaling and divisor-pushforward properties of `ConstantReduction`); the hypothesis `hR₀` that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\overline{M}$, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$; an index $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$); a family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $F$ indexed by the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb Z/q$; and a family $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ of valuation subrings of $F$ indexed by $W$.
--
--   The Igusa hypotheses are: `hIg_inf`, which identifies $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ at the line `lineInfty q` as the Gauss ring, $f \in O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ if and only if there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero coefficientwise reduction and $f \cdot y = x$ in Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; `hIg`, which provides for each line $\ell$ some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with `redQ q γ • lineInfty q = ℓ` and $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, injectivity of $\ell \mapsto O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$; and `hIg_perm`, which says that for every index $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the pullbacks along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$.
--
--   The supersingular hypotheses are: `hSS_A`, that a constant from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ exactly when it lies in $A$; `hSS_over`, that for $s \in W$ and $f \in$ `R₀.integers` which is regular at every place $P$ of $\overline{M}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the class of `coeffEmb` applied to `jq` is regular (that is, $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(j)$ implies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$), and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in $F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and moreover for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value at $s$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of the image of $f$ and the constant $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$; `hSS_fix`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all $\zeta'$ and all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contains an element $t$ such that $t - a$ is a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a \in A$.
--
--   Further, $R$ is a regular prolongation of $F$ along $A$ with values in `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, with `hR` asserting `R.integers = OIg (lineInfty q)`, and `hR₀O` asserting that $f \in$ `R₀.integers` if and only if its image in $F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$.
--
--   The arithmetic hypotheses on the base are: an element $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$; a subfield $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ with $\pi_0 \in A$, such that $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is a henselian local ring, and has algebraically closed residue field (`hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres`), together with `hκ`: every $a \in A$ is congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Next, an auxiliary prime $\ell$ with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; and $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally, a finite extension $K_1$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and a valuation subring $A_1 \subseteq K_1$ with $A_1 = A \cap K_1$ (`hA₁`), which is a discrete valuation ring and a henselian local ring.
--
--   The conclusion is stated for $F$ regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q} \to F$, and asserts the following for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $F/k_0$ subject to four conditions: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by all constants from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of $F$; $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for every index $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; a linear disjointness condition, namely that for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to F$ with all $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the $K'$-linear independence of $c$ and the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ force $a_i = 0$ for all $i$; and $F_0$ contains every element of $F$ whose Laurent series lies in the image of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`, i.e. has rational coefficients.
--
--   Write $T_1$ for the compositum, inside $F$, of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_1$. The assertion is made for any $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map sends $a \in A_1$ to the constant attached to $a \in K_1 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$, and for any $j_1 \in T_1$ whose image in $F$ is the class of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` under the inclusion given by `hle`, with $j_1 \ne 0$; and for any finite set $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of places of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` over `ResidueField A` for which there exists a ring homomorphism $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` to that field such that, first, for every $f \in$ `R₀.integers` the image of $f$ in $F$ lies in `R.integers` with $R$-residue $j$ applied to the $R_0$-residue of $f$, and second, $Q \in N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ if and only if there is $s \in W$ with $g$ in the valuation subring of $s$ precisely when $j(g)$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, for all $g$.
--
--   The scheme in question is $\mathfrak X_1 :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout gluing $X_{\mathrm{fin}} = \operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra `chartAlgFin` of elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$ and $X_\infty = \operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgInf`, the elements integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$, along the middle chart. Six abbreviations are introduced. For a point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ and $f \in T_1$: `InStalk x f` says that for every point $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ with `ιFin`-image $x$ there are $g,h$ in `chartAlgFin` with $h \notin y$ and $f h = g$ in $T_1$, and likewise over $X_\infty$ with `chartAlgInf`; `InMax x f` is the same with the additional requirement $g \in y$ in both clauses. For a place $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, `Centred P x` says that $P$ is rational and that every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation subring of $P$, has $P$-value in $A$, and that this value has $A$-valuation $< 1$ exactly when `InMax x f`. Next, `GoodPt x` is the conjunction of five clauses: the structure morphism `toBase` sends $x$ to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$; $x$ specialises only to itself; for every $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ over $x$, every element of `chartAlgFin` whose image in $F$ is a non-unit of `R.integers` lies in the prime of $y$, and the same over $X_\infty$; and for every $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y$, the value $\varphi(j_1)$ (on the coordinate `jChartFin`) does not lie in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7). For a place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, `Reads x Q` says that every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in `R.integers`, that its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and that this residue is a non-unit there exactly when `InMax x f`. Finally, `OffBranch x` says that for every line $\ell \ne$ `lineInfty q` and every $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ over $x$ there is an element of `chartAlgFin` whose image in $F$ is a non-unit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ and which is not in the prime of $y$, and likewise over $X_\infty$.
--
--   The conclusion asserted is a single statement: for every point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ satisfying `GoodPt x`, there exists a place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` over `ResidueField A` with `Reads x Q`. The abbreviations `Centred` and `OffBranch` are introduced in the statement but do not occur in this conclusion.
--
--   This is the existence half of the reading dictionary on the $\infty$-Igusa leg of the semistable covering of the modular curve at $q = 2$: a closed point of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model which lies on the $\infty$-Igusa component and is not supersingular in $j$ determines a place of the reduced Igusa function field compatibly with the stalk at that point. It is the $q = 2$ companion of the corresponding statement for $q \ge 5$, and it feeds [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.reads_unique_and_exists_offBranch_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.reads_unique_and_exists_offBranch_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_two), where the place so produced is shown to be unique and the point is placed off the other branches.
